  "findings": [
    "All three methods executed all 14 tests in every final evaluation cycle; verdicts, observations and modeled total costs matched for each cycle.",
    "Discovery averages exclude cycles with no observed failure; those cycles are counted separately.",
    "The final cohort introduces timeout behavior unseen during fitting and validation, then ends with independent mixed scenarios where history is less informative.",
    "Lowest mean modeled cost to first failure: Recent failures first (148.956 modeled ms). This is an observed simulation result, not a promised ML gain."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The scenario schedule and device are synthetic; real-lab transfer is unmeasured.",
    "A defect-free history cannot predict a genuinely new defect with certainty.",
    "Test order changes feedback timing, not the work of executing the full suite.",
    "The simple rule may beat ML; two fixed C values are the entire tuning budget.",
    "Only the selected fault scenarios are exercised; this is not a coverage percentage.",
    "Failure probability scores are not independently calibrated confidence estimates."
  ],
